{
  "id": "28247_tsutau",
  "headword": "{伝|つた}う",
  "reading": "つたう",
  "romaji": "tsutau",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to go along; to run down (a surface)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to move along; to run down (following a surface)",
      "explanation": "To move along the length of something, using it as a path or support. Often used of liquid (tears, sweat, rain) running down a surface, or of a person making their way along a wall, rope, or ledge. The surface followed is marked with を."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28247_tsutau_ex1",
      "japanese": "{涙|なみだ}が{頬|ほお}を{伝|つた}う。",
      "english": "Tears run down the cheeks.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28247_tsutau_ex2",
      "japanese": "{汗|あせ}が{背中|せなか}を{伝|つた}って{落|お}ちた。",
      "english": "Sweat ran down my back and dripped off.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28247_tsutau_ex3",
      "japanese": "{壁|かべ}を{伝|つた}って{暗|くら}い{廊下|ろうか}を{進|すす}んだ。",
      "english": "I made my way down the dark hallway feeling along the wall.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Takes を to mark the surface followed, but describes movement along it rather than acting on it. Tagged transitive.\n- Pattern: Xが{場所|ばしょ}を{伝|つた}う\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {涙|なみだ}が{頬|ほお}を{伝|つた}う: tears run down the cheeks\n- {壁|かべ}を{伝|つた}う: feel one's way along a wall\n- {雨水|あまみず}が{窓|まど}を{伝|つた}う: rainwater trickles down the window\n\nUSAGE:\nDo not confuse with {伝|つた}わる (to be transmitted, to be conveyed) or {伝|つた}える (to convey). {伝|つた}う is specifically physical movement along a surface.",
